-- title:
--   Product of the component ideal sheaves on Y equals (p)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{X}$ for $p$ (the bundled proper flat integral normal model `DRModel p` together with its rational and geometric curve models, its cusp sections, its smooth locus and the two components `compInf`, `compZero` of the special fibre). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Assume the node index type [`V3Glue.Site.Node p 𝔛 κ`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L43), the underlying space of the pullback of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ along $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$, is a finite type, and let $H$ be the site hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267): finiteness of the nodes, existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of the assignment of a point `xpt` to each node, closedness of each such point, and the model hypotheses for $O$. Let $\xi$ be the two distinguished points and assume each $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input $C$, i.e. in the complement of the finitely many node points. The conclusion: for every affine open $U$ of the glued resolution $Y$, the product over all $v$ in `X0MqComponents (width …)` of the ideal sheaf data `comp v`, evaluated at $U$, is the ideal of $\Gamma(Y, U)$ generated by the image of $p$.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model is the divisor $(p)$, written as the product of the ideal sheaves of its irreducible components on every affine open of the glued scheme; equivalently, the components occur with multiplicity one and their sum cuts out the fibre. It is one of the fields verified in the construction of the resolved model with its étale crossing charts, used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts).
